-## The season's colour for grass and open ground; in winter, snow lies on it instead.
+## Winter's snow on the land, in Terrain3D's own shader: an even cover on all
+## ground that faces up, thinner where the earth is dark (roads, trodden mud,
+## ploughed fields show through, as in Manor Lords), settling and melting over
+## half a season. It replaces swapping the grass texture for snow, which left
+## the dirt and fields bare in blotches.
+const SNOW_UNIFORMS := "uniform float snow_cover = 0.0;\nuniform vec3 snow_col = vec3(0.9, 0.92, 0.95);\n"
+const SNOW_LINE := "\n\t{ float up = smoothstep(0.78, 0.97, v_normal.y); float lum = dot(ALBEDO, vec3(0.3333)); float bare = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.1, 0.3, lum); ALBEDO = mix(ALBEDO, snow_col * (0.92 + 0.08 * lum), snow_cover * up * (1.0 - 0.65 * bare)); }"
+var _snow_now := 0.0
+
+
+## The season's colour for grass and open ground; in winter, snow settles over all of it.
